{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1514892-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth","id":1514892,"title":"Ritual of Sacred Rebirth","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-13T15:51:51-07:00","id":1514892,"title":"Ritual of Sacred Rebirth","content":"In WoD the Ritual of Sacred Rebirth enables a kinfolk that slays and skins 5 Garou to steal their changing gift and become Garou themselves. <br /> <br /> I was wondering if anyone has ever ported it over to Forsaken and if so what did you do with it? I don't think the Skin Dancers becoming a full tribe is very realistic, but possibly a small lodge would be doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T16:06:43-07:00","id":1514893,"title":"","content":"From my cursory understanding of Forsaken, one can become a Wolfblooded by enough exposure to Lunacy (though that does risk insanity), and any Wolfblooded has the potential to go through the First Change. I could be wrong though.<br /> <br /> Not <i>exactly</i> what you asked, but there's precedent for mundanes becoming supernaturals","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T16:40:28-07:00","id":1514896,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t recall seeing homebrew, but I can see a potential one involving idigam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T01:28:07-07:00","id":1514927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1514892-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth?p=1514893#post1514893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my cursory understanding of Forsaken, one can become a Wolfblooded by enough exposure to Lunacy (though that does risk insanity), and any Wolfblooded has the potential to go through the First Change. I could be wrong though.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is unofficial Bonus/Minus to Lunacy by being bitten by Uratha to get Dramatic Failure on Lunacy - that's one of effects is becoming Wolf-Blooded. And from this, to First Change then. In that model, ritual could be unnecessary - <b><i>much easier</i></b> is to be bitten by Uratha, heal up wounds, being bitten once more, etc. than going for 5 Uratha skinning. Just saying. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But if you want skinning Uratha to be a thing - go for it, there is enough canon to support much easier roads to werewolfness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>'WtF 2E, p. 102</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>SPONTANEOUS WOLF-BLOODED</b><br /> Sometimes, just sometimes, Wolf-Blooded arise from the taint of Lunacy, not from genetics. Any time a human suffers a dramatic failure on the Lunacy breaking point roll, she becomes Wolf-Blooded. This doesn\u2019t take instantly. It occurs at a seemingly random moon phase over the course of the next lunar month. This disproportionately favors the auspice of the Uratha she witnessed. As the change slowly overtakes her, she becomes Wolf-Blooded, with a Tell and all the other defining traits of the blood. She also becomes eligible to purchase Wolf-Blooded Merits. See Appendix One for rules on Wolf-Blooded characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-14-2023, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T21:33:30-07:00","id":1515717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1514892-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth?p=1514927#post1514927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is unofficial Bonus/Minus to Lunacy by being bitten by Uratha to get Dramatic Failure on Lunacy - that's one of effects is becoming Wolf-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>The effects of a mortal suffering wound penalties and having had lethal damage done to them by the werewolf inflicting Lunacy on them specifically make it <i>less</i> likely that the survivor of a werewolf attack will become Wolf-Blooded as the same knock-on effect that lets a coordinated group of witnesses act with their wits about them. The Spontaneous Wolf-Blooded mechanics are such that, between the way the bonuses and penalties work, the way werewolf culture treats letting their activities be known to outside humans, and the delay in acquiring a Tell, the average character has no reason to suspect that an event <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/662321-making-wolf-bloods?p=667286#post667286\">they remember as clearly as someone who normally failed their Lunacy check would</a> has anything to do with their growing teeth or seeing dead people a week or four later.<br /> <br /> <br /> Pack Rites working how they do, you could probably adapt something using the material on Shadow Occultists from Shunned by the Moon and/or the Merit-based update to Skinthieves from the Beneath the Skin Dark Era (p248-249 of DE1), albeit the result will probably be a variant of the werewolf template rather than a standard Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T04:39:03-07:00","id":1516632,"title":"","content":"I feel as though the main reason you wouldn't have something that straight up copies the ritual from Apocalypse is that it's ultimately a power rooted in the dramatic interplay between kinfolk and Garou. Something that jumps off of the element of kinfolk as people of the bloodline that didn't get to become actual werewolves, and might have some resentment for the missed opportunity and the second class status they're relegated to.<br /> <br /> I find that Forsaken severely downplays the element of Wolf-Blooded being directly related to werewolves and essentially removes any of the social dynamics of feeling as though it was something they could have had (as well as making them a bit less of an oppressed underclass), so the thematic foundations for such a ritual aren't there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T07:20:34-07:00","id":1516644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1514892-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth?p=1516632#post1516632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though the main reason you wouldn't have something that straight up copies the ritual from Apocalypse is that it's ultimately a power rooted in the dramatic interplay between kinfolk and Garou. Something that jumps off of the element of kinfolk as people of the bloodline that didn't get to become actual werewolves, and might have some resentment for the missed opportunity and the second class status they're relegated to.<br /> <br /> I find that Forsaken severely downplays the element of Wolf-Blooded being directly related to werewolves and essentially removes any of the social dynamics of feeling as though it was something they could have had (as well as making them a bit less of an oppressed underclass), so the thematic foundations for such a ritual aren't there.</div> </div> </div> </div>WtF does downplay it over all, but it's still there if a DM chooses to use it and I kind of think it could almost work better in Forsaken. <br /> <br /> Picture this, you're a normal mortal out for a stroll with your wife and child until a freaking werewolf interrupts. You're able to get away with your child but it kills your wife. Even as you deal with her loss, you notice you're beginning to change and then boom, a few weeks later you get angry, more angry than you've ever been, you change forms and end up killing your child. Then, your life in tatters, yourself scarcely deserving to be called human, the people who mattered the most to you dead, one at the claws of a monster and one at your own hands, the very monster who killed your wife and caused your transformation shows up, over joyed to discover what you've become, tells you that you've been chosen by godlike beings and you're now kind of like him, but much less and forever trapped as less than. You've lost everything and you get to watch mere teenagers elevated above you due to the accident of their birth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T09:23:19-07:00","id":1516661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1514892-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth?p=1516644#post1516644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WtF does downplay it over all, but it's still there if a DM chooses to use it and I kind of think it could almost work better in Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Picture this, you're a normal mortal out for a stroll with your wife and child until a freaking werewolf interrupts. You're able to get away with your child but it kills your wife. Even as you deal with her loss, you notice you're beginning to change and then boom, a few weeks later you get angry, more angry than you've ever been, you change forms and end up killing your child. Then, your life in tatters, yourself scarcely deserving to be called human, the people who mattered the most to you dead, one at the claws of a monster and one at your own hands, the very monster who killed your wife and caused your transformation shows up, over joyed to discover what you've become, tells you that you've been chosen by godlike beings and you're now kind of like him, but much less and forever trapped as less than. You've lost everything and you get to watch mere teenagers elevated above you due to the accident of their birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spontaneous Wolf-Blooded do not retain clear memories of the event whose Lunacy triggered their acquisition of a Tell any more than a regular failure or success on the roll. If there's any connection the character would draw it would be entirely unconscious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T06:21:26-07:00","id":1517482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1514892-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth?p=1516644#post1516644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Picture this, you're a normal mortal out for a stroll with your wife and child until a freaking werewolf interrupts. You're able to get away with your child but it kills your wife. Even as you deal with her loss, you notice you're beginning to change and then boom, a few weeks later you get angry, more angry than you've ever been, you change forms and end up killing your child. Then, your life in tatters, yourself scarcely deserving to be called human, the people who mattered the most to you dead, one at the claws of a monster and one at your own hands, the very monster who killed your wife and caused your transformation shows up, over joyed to discover what you've become, tells you that you've been chosen by godlike beings and you're now kind of like him, but much less and forever trapped as less than. You've lost everything and you get to watch mere teenagers elevated above you due to the accident of their birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does this extremely specific and singular character want to go full werewolf?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T08:20:51-07:00","id":1517493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1514892-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth?p=1517482#post1517482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why does this extremely specific and singular character want to go full werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't all characters &quot;extremely specific and singular?&quot; If not they absolutely should be. Try it in your next game. (Also, this extremely specific and singular character is what is known as an example.)<br /> <br /> But he's angry at being forced into a lower station, angry that others, less competent and less experienced are above him in the social order for how they were born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T09:12:07-07:00","id":1517496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1514892-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth?p=1517493#post1517493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't all characters &quot;extremely specific and singular?&quot; If not they absolutely should be. Try it in your next game. (Also, this extremely specific and singular character is what is known as an example.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bad example, for the reasons discussed above \u2014 the extremely specific circumstances necessary for a spontaneous Wolf-Blooded and the werewolf who triggered their condition to piece together the reason for their Tell beggar belief, between the random timing involved, the operative amnesia, and the strong inclination of werewolves both culturally and spiritually toward ensuring no mortal witnesses survive to tell the tale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T10:23:09-07:00","id":1517501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1514892-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth?p=1517496#post1517496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a bad example, for the reasons discussed above</div> </div> </div> </div>That's your opinion and you are welcome to it. You know what is said about opinions?<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2014 the extremely specific circumstances necessary for a spontaneous Wolf-Blooded and the werewolf who triggered their condition to piece together the reason for their Tell beggar belief, </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, in a game about werewolves it's the person who remembers running into the werewolf that beggars belief. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> between the random timing involved, the operative amnesia, and the strong inclination of werewolves both culturally and spiritually toward ensuring no mortal witnesses survive to tell the tale. </div> </div> </div>Except, of course, if &quot;no witnesses survived to tell the tale&quot; there would never be spontaneous wolf-blooded, would there? So clearly witnesses do survive and do so in sufficient numbers that the author made it a point to include something that happens to a tiny percent of surviving witnesses. <br /> <br /> You're welcome to dislike the idea, you're welcome to not use the idea, but if you don't have anything positive to add or suggest then you're also welcome to not post on the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T11:05:45-07:00","id":1517505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1514892-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth?p=1517501#post1517501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yes, in a game about werewolves it's the person who remembers running into the werewolf that beggars belief.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a setting where &quot;people who see a werewolf don't remember it clearly as being a werewolf encounter unless they get a roll result that has a 50/50 chance on a dicepool of triple the stats of an average person&quot; and &quot;the more potent a werewolf you are and the more monstrous the form you're in, the less likely a witness is to succeed at the roll that affects how they remember the scene where they saw you&quot; are both true? <i>Yes.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except, of course, if &quot;no witnesses survived to tell the tale&quot; there would never be spontaneous wolf-blooded, would there? So clearly witnesses do survive and do so in sufficient numbers that the author made it a point to include something that happens to a tiny percent of surviving witnesses. </div> </div> </div>The surviving witnesses don't remember it if they became a spontaneous wolf-blooded, which means they're not going to be telling the tale about surviving a werewolf encounter and drawing the attention of werewolves looking to clean up after themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're welcome to dislike the idea, you're welcome to not use the idea, but if you don't have anything positive to add or suggest then you're also welcome to not post on the idea. </div> </div> </div>I made my suggestion and then you put forth a hypothetical that directly ignored the writer citation I provided explaining that spontaneous Wolf-Blooded aren't going to remember the thing that caused them to become Wolf-Blooded. Given that I have seenmultiple occasions of people asking why the Spontaneous Wolf-Blooded mechanics aren't exploited by werewolves, I am inclined to stop this bit of misinformation from propagating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Typo corrections. 07-08-2023, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T10:49:31-07:00","id":1517795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1514892-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth?p=1517493#post1517493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't all characters &quot;extremely specific and singular?&quot; If not they absolutely should be. Try it in your next game. (Also, this extremely specific and singular character is what is known as an example.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It means that it excludes much that would give applicability to the Ritual to any character besides the one you've put forwards.<br /> <br /> Which it barely has in the first place.<br /> <br /> When I say &quot;extremely specific and singular&quot; I mean in the same way as when a person tries to create the most outlandishly curated example to try and justify something that couldn't be justified with something more general. &quot;What if there was a meteor about to hit the Earth, and the only way to stop it was beating up an adorable puppy, would that be unethical&quot; kind of thing.<br /> <br /> This is in contrast to my point that in Werewolf: the Apocalypse, resentment of Garou by Kinfolk is a systemic thing with deep cultural roots from which one can draw a variety of characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But he's angry at being forced into a lower station, angry that others, less competent and less experienced are above him in the social order for how they were born.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that very generic, not particularly rooted in the dynamics between Wolf-Blooded and Uratha otherwise posited in the game, and rather internally contradictory. Like, encountering a werewolf devastated his life, but he still sees it as something worth valuing enough to resent the idea of others having it better?<br /> <br /> Like, your grimdark backstory does not particularly convey competence and experience to me.<br /> <br /> The assumption that newly Changed werewolves would be teenagers is also something I think is incongruous with Forsaken in general and Second Edition in particular. Bloodlines seem to have been dramatically downplayed by now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T11:56:58-07:00","id":1517800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1514892-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth?p=1517795#post1517795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I say &quot;extremely specific and singular&quot; I mean in the same way as when a person tries to create the most outlandishly curated example to try and justify something that couldn't be justified with something more general. &quot;What if there was a meteor about to hit the Earth, and the only way to stop it was beating up an adorable puppy, would that be unethical&quot; kind of thing.<br /> <br /> This is in contrast to my point that in Werewolf: the Apocalypse, resentment of Garou by Kinfolk is a systemic thing with deep cultural roots from which one can draw a variety of characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of what you meant, my point was more of there are a ton of reasons to resent the Uratha as well if you use your imagination. <br /> <br /> I will also point out that this forum is full of &quot;extremely specific and singular&quot; creations, like a hive-claimed ghost blooded tyrant. Do you call all of them out as such? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I find that very generic, not particularly rooted in the dynamics between Wolf-Blooded and Uratha otherwise posited in the game, and rather internally contradictory. Like, encountering a werewolf devastated his life, but he still sees it as something worth valuing enough to resent the idea of others having it better? </div> </div> </div>In real life people often hold many contradictory beliefs and you will see that many times the abused become abusers. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The assumption that newly Changed werewolves would be teenagers is also something I think is incongruous with Forsaken in general and Second Edition in particular. </div> </div> </div>Other than the consistent use of &quot;young&quot; to describe newly changed werewolves, which could imply young as a werewolf rather than years of age there isn't a whole lot to dictate age in the rules as far as I can tell. But there are other arguments for the change coming at a young age, such as the examples include someone spending the night in a scary house and someone else sneaking out then worrying about their mom being mad are both strong examples of the change coming in early teen years. The third example is of someone who is in the &quot;go out and party&quot; phase changing, which could be some later in life, but I'd be surprised if it was much after 21 though the text isn't specific. The next example talks about &quot;staying out late for a school project&quot; so again a young teen most likely. The last example takes place in a bar where the young Uratha went out with friends, so likely young adult. <br /> <br /> What evidence did you have to present that newly changing werewolves aren't often teenagers? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bloodlines seem to have been dramatically downplayed by now. </div> </div> </div>They're still there though, and the easiest way to be wolf blooded is still be born to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T13:24:33-07:00","id":1517813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1514892-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth?p=1517800#post1517800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will also point out that this forum is full of &quot;extremely specific and singular&quot; creations, like a hive-claimed ghost blooded tyrant. Do you call all of them out as such?</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is between coming up with a form of antagonist and trying to answer the question of &quot;does this piece of magic have the same narrative resonance as it did in its original context&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In real life people often hold many contradictory beliefs and you will see that many times the abused become abusers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's technically accurate, but as a narrative proposition it isn't really developed, and considering the graphic and intense nature of what you put ahead of &quot;a Wolf-Blooded might also resent werewolves&quot; it just ends up coming across as gratuitous.<br /> <br /> What value is there in this character concept of &quot;person who inadvertently savagely killed their child&quot;, both in general terms and to provide an inroad for a ritual for people to make themselves Uratha?<br /> <br /> At the very least you could have offered something like a person in some state where they feel that the only way such horror could be worth it is if they go all the way into the full form that can then do some things of significance. But it was just &quot;werewolf kills wife, widower kills baby, is angry at privileged youths&quot;. It's such a non-sequitur.<br /> <br /> Or hell, maybe a spontaneous Wolf-Blooded whose backstory is less about absurd ultraviolence and more about being drawn into a society that they never asked for where they find themselves expected to facilitate the needs of the Uratha. Perhaps could be a person who, prior to becoming Wolf-Blooded, was a bit of a bigshot among mortals, and being forced into a relationship where somebody else are at the top of the pyramid troubles them.<br /> <br /> Just something with a bit more continuity to the idea and that put the question of &quot;is horrific child murder necessary here&quot; through a few more drafts.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T13:31:40-07:00","id":1517814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1514892-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth?p=1517813#post1517813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difference is between coming up with a form of antagonist and trying to answer the question of &quot;does this piece of magic have the same narrative resonance as it did in its original context&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, your comment was referencing the antagonist I brought up, not the ritual itself so tryy again? Also, while trying again, please tell me your sources on werewolves undergoing the first change not in their teen years, you must have accidentally deleted that question. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's technically accurate, but as a narrative proposition it isn't really developed, and considering the graphic and intense nature of what you put ahead of &quot;a Wolf-Blooded might also resent werewolves&quot; it just ends up coming across as gratuitous.<br /> <br /> What value is there in this character concept of &quot;person who inadvertently savagely killed their child&quot;, both in general terms and to provide an inroad for a ritual for people to make themselves Uratha?<br /> <br /> At the very least you could have offered something like a person in some state where they feel that the only way such horror could be worth it is if they go all the way into the full form that can then do some things of significance. But it was just &quot;werewolf kills wife, widower kills baby, is angry at privileged youths&quot;. It's such a non-sequitur.<br /> <br /> Or hell, maybe a spontaneous Wolf-Blooded whose backstory is less about absurd ultraviolence and more about being drawn into a society that they never asked for where they find themselves expected to facilitate the needs of the Uratha. Perhaps could be a person who, prior to becoming Wolf-Blooded, was a bit of a bigshot among mortals, and being forced into a relationship where somebody else are at the top of the pyramid troubles them.<br /> <br /> Just something with a bit more continuity to the idea<br /> </div> </div> </div>The NPC was a stream of conscience answer to you arguing that the wolfblooded don't have conflict with the Uratha in the way the kinfolk do. The point of this thread is the ritual, not the NPC. The point of the NPC was that there's plenty of reasons to have created the ritual and to provide an example of who might have done it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and that put the question of &quot;is horrific child murder necessary here&quot; through a few more drafts. </div> </div> </div>I think we've come to the crux of your problem with the NPC right here. You're welcome to concede that there's plenty of reasons that a wolf-blooded, or even a human, might wish to go to extreme lengths in order to transform into a member of the Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}